<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH FIN MIN HAS NO COMMENT ON KPN STAKE.</title>
<headline>DUTCH FIN MIN HAS NO COMMENT ON KPN STAKE.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch Finance Ministry said on Tuesday it had no comment on what it planned to do with its 45 percent stake in post and telecoms giant KPN, which earlier announced plans to split into two units next year.</p>
<p>&quot;If we had any opinion on this, we wouldn't say so in advance. We have no comment,&quot; a spokeswoman told Reuters.</p>
<p>KPN chairman Wim Dik earlier confirmed the firm would seek separate listings for its telecoms and postal units in the first half of 1998, in a move aimed at focusing shareholders' interests.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
